.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1252 PM PST Fri Nov 27 2026
(This evening through Saturday night)

If you`ve been out and about today shopping or just post holiday
hiking you probably noticed the nice weather. Similar to
yesterday, morning fog dissipated giving way to some high clouds
streaming over the region. Temperatures will once again top out
in the 60s to low 70s, which is above normal for late November.
That being said, given the nice weather and people heading to the
coast potentially, keep in mind we still have hazardous
conditions along area beaches. See BEACHES below for more detail.

Should note some of the high clouds moving into the North Bay have
a cu like vibe. In fact, KMUX is actually picking up a few high
level echoes over the northern coastal waters. Not expecting any
precip with these clouds, but some virga is definitely possible.

The longwave pattern over the next 24-36 hours will continue to
be dominated by ridge of high pressure aloft. As such, expect more
of the same:patchy fog night/morning, mild afternoon temps, and
more high clouds ahead of the next system.

