(00Z TAFS)
Issued at 312 PM PST Fri Nov 27 2026

VFR conditions with high clouds and light to gentle flow, generally
offshore, through the evening hours. Low to moderate confidence of
fog and stratus development at the North Bay and interior East Bay
valleys tonight, with large-scle offshore flow helping to keep the
atmosphere dry and increasing forecast uncertainty through Saturday
morning. Light to gentle offshore winds resume Saturday afternoon.

Vicinity of SFO... Moderate to high confidence of VFR through the
TAF period with some mist possible Saturday morning. Winds remain
light and gentle, generally from the north to the northeast.
Stratus development is possible right at the end of the TAF
period.

SFO Bridge Approach... Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals... VFR through the TAF period. Light to
gentle northwest winds into the evening, with offshore drainage flow
overnight into Saturday morning.

